WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.058
- Oh my gosh! You're a
vision, this is so beautiful.

00:00:03.058 --> 00:00:04.810
- Oh thank you, this is
my meeting pigs outfit,

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.827
I knew there was gonna be
pigs here, so I was like,

00:00:06.827 --> 00:00:07.660
"I have to pull out the best dress."

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.250
- I think they saw what you look like

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.867
and they were like, "No, she
looks too pretty for pigs"

00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:12.515
"to be like sniffing on you."

00:00:12.515 --> 00:00:13.348
- They were so adorable.

00:00:13.348 --> 00:00:15.651
- They were so cute, they
do not like to be held.

00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:16.950
(audience laughs)

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.700
Yeah, that's when the
velociraptor sound comes out

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.180
when you're held, yeah.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.748
Have you ever met Joel? Have you ever met?

00:00:22.748 --> 00:00:23.581
- We just did.

00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:24.570
- [Kelly] You just did.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.723
- I was in "Suicide Squad" though.

00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:27.110
(audience laughs)

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.410
- No I was, but I would have been amazing.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.810
So wait we were just
talking about time machine,

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.030
so if you could go past
future, like whatever,

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:35.863
if you could do whatever,

00:00:35.863 --> 00:00:36.930
what would you do with a time machine?

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.600
- Oh I think I would go
back and meet my ancestors

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.270
and see where I came from.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.360
- [Kelly] Really? That's cool.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.430
- Yeah, my family and my
lineage of ancestors and people.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.468
- [Kelly] See if
ancestry.com got it right?

00:00:48.468 --> 00:00:50.263
- Exactly! 'Cause sometimes
it's a little iffy.

00:00:50.263 --> 00:00:52.167
- I know I'm always
like, "How am I getting,"

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.250
"how's it changing? How's
my percentage going?"

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.083
I'm like, "Wait what?"

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.610
- Everyday I get an email like
you have new DNA relatives,

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:58.443
I'm like, "How is that even possible?"

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:00.980
- Like today I'm super Irish.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.940
Yesterday I was like more English.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.790
I'm like, yeah, I don't know.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.460
- I wanna goo see it for myself.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.130
- That's cool, I like that.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.180
Well, your show sounds awesome.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.890
So can you tell everybody a little bit

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:12.977
what it's about if they haven't seen it?

00:01:12.977 --> 00:01:14.410
- "Euphoria".
- Yes, "Euphoria".

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:17.800
Yeah, "Euphoria" is an incredible show

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.800
that is depicting what young
people are going through

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.490
in this day and age, even though
some of the content matter

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.950
may be rough and it may be hard.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.450
- Rough meaning like it's just real.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.800
- It's just real, exactly,
it may be hard to watch

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.750
but I always sit in a space of gratitude

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.790
and being empathetic towards our show

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.180
because you have to realize
there are real people

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.239
going through these situations

00:01:42.239 --> 00:01:43.780
and I might not be going through it,

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.240
but my peers and my friends

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.430
and my acquaintances.
- And you should enlighten it.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.380
- Exactly, so that's why I'm so grateful

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.210
to be a part of "Euphoria",
season two is wild

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.010
if y'all thought season one was crazy,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.156
I don't know what you're
gonna to do with season two.

00:01:56.156 --> 00:01:57.820
(audience laughs)

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.400
But it's a really fun
show to be a part of,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.650
I get to work with my big sister Z, so--

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.483
- She was just on here.

00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:04.510
- I know, somebody told
me, yeah I love her.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.560
- We caught her 'cause
they had to go on Zoom

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.080
and so we caught her, she
was in a real pretty dress

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.683
and then one of the cameras
caught her pants underneath.

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.516
(audience laughs)

00:02:12.516 --> 00:02:14.660
It was like her workout
pants, it was awesome.(laughs)

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.470
- Yeah, she's an incredible human,

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.320
so I get to work with
some really great people

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.100
and be a part of a really cool show.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.140
- What a cool life you have, oh my gosh!

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.303
So Drake is a producer of the
show, I did not know that.

00:02:26.303 --> 00:02:28.440
So how involved is he? Is he involved?

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.823
- No, he's really involved,

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.020
we were doing table reads for season two

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.690
a couple of months back.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.580
And of course, like
you're not expecting Drake

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.113
to be at your table read.

00:02:39.113 --> 00:02:40.720
- You're expecting him to
be on tour, busy, yeah.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.100
- Exactly, like performing somewhere

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.830
in his big old house in Canada.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.980
And I pull up to the lot

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.080
and he's there with all
of his homies, it's him

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.220
and then his business
partner, future, the prince

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.870
and they literally sat through,

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.030
I think it was a three hour table read

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.310
'cause we went through
a couple of episodes

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:03.360
and he was so involved and so in tune

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.410
and you don't really
expect that from a person,

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.360
I know that he's a brilliant
businessman and creative,

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.900
but I mean he's Drake,

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.250
he doesn't really have to pay attention

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.083
in the table read and he did.

00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:15.600
- [Kelly] I mean that's cool though, yeah.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.590
- Yeah, but he did come from
acting, so it makes sense.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:18.423
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:18.423 --> 00:03:20.500
- Yeah, he did, I didn't know
that, but in Canada he did,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.390
I didn't know that either.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.603
- Yeah, "Degrassi" is a very similar show.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.215
(audience laughs)

00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:26.350
Canadian show.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.980
- I know, I didn't know,
that's when he told me that

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.050
and I was like, "Oh! I had no idea,"

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.540
I only knew him because of his music

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.050
but that's cool, all right.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.560
I love that he didn't
just slap his name on it,

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.026
that he's involved with it, that's cool.

00:03:35.026 --> 00:03:35.859
- Exactly, that's really cool.

00:03:35.859 --> 00:03:38.485
- He doesn't interrupt and go
like, "You're doing it wrong."

00:03:38.485 --> 00:03:39.318
(audience laughs)

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:40.440
- No, he's so in tune

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.630
and of course I was kind
of like looking at him

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.660
to see if he was actually paying attention

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.330
and turning his pages

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.300
and you could tell he was
feeling all the emotion,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.710
I was like, "Okay Drake."

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.560
- That's so cool.

00:03:52.507 --> 00:03:53.340
And it makes you feel good too

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.075
that he's really into your
project that he's doing,

00:03:55.075 --> 00:03:55.908
that so cool.

